SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-here
FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS=serviceAccountKey.json
JWT_SECRET_KEY=your-jwt-secret-key-here

# ============================================
# VERCEL DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
# For Vercel deployment, set these as Environment Variables
# in your Vercel project dashboard (Settings > Environment Variables):
#
# 1. SECRET_KEY: Your secret key for Flask (min 32 chars)
# 2. JWT_SECRET_KEY: Your JWT secret key (min 32 chars)
# 3. FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS: Paste the ENTIRE content of 
#    serviceAccountKey.json as a single-line JSON string
#
# How to set FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS on Vercel:
#   1. Open your serviceAccountKey.json file
#   2. Copy ALL content (the entire JSON)
#   3. Go to Vercel Dashboard > Your Project > Settings > Environment Variables
#   4. Add new variable: FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS
#   5. Paste the entire JSON content as the value
#   6. Make sure it's set for "Production" environment
#
# IMPORTANT: The .env file and serviceAccountKey.json are NOT
# deployed to Vercel (they're in .gitignore). You MUST set
# these environment variables in the Vercel dashboard!
#
# Example (DO NOT use this value, use your own):
# FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS={"type":"service_account","project_id":"your-project",...}
# ============================================